  "eyebrow": "Data Point 04 · Throughput at load",
  "headline": {
    "lead": "Under load, the FPGA's edge is",
    "accent": " small payloads at high request rate."
  },
  "lede": "Three regimes, one honest sweep. On small, frequent payloads — the common inline-guardrail case — Themis sustains up to 1.7× RE2's throughput with a 2.5× tighter p99, and holds flat where RE2's tail climbs. As payloads grow the gap narrows to parity, and on large payloads both engines are bandwidth-bound. All three are below — read the whole curve.",
